  "result": "I made three edits to fix the seat accounting. I did not run the test suite, since the task asked for edits only.\n\n- **Removal frees the seat immediately** (`src/server/services/usage-service.ts`): `registerUsageListeners` now subscribes to `member.removed` and decrements `seatsUsed` by 1, mirroring the existing `member.joined` increment.\n- **Recount counts only current members** (`src/server/repositories/usage-repository.ts`): `recomputeUsage` now counts only `members` rows with `status = 'active'` and `archivedAt IS NULL`. Before, it counted every row, including removed ones.\n- **Only pending invitations hold seats** (`src/server/repositories/invitation-repository.ts`): `countPendingInvitations` now also excludes revoked invitations. Revoking an invitation, and the revoke step inside `resendInvitation`, now give the seat back.\n\nExpired-but-unaccepted, unrevoked invitations still count as pending, because the spec only excludes accepted and revoked ones.",
